# L §5.7 (round 12): "a key that enters only plain kinds has as base the kind of its earliest entry, by known, then by
# its lifespan's start"; "Two ... earliest plain entries tied on both, are refused (LOAD-DUP)". q: ana enters
# volunteers (known 2026-01-01) and members (known 2026-02-01): base volunteers, and things of a kind compare "in the
# order they entered, then by key" (L §4.2), so both are counted in each kind on their days. r: bo enters two plain kinds
# in one version with one lifespan: refused. (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.7, writer 5's T-46.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind volunteers
kind members

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  volunteers + [ana] lives 2026-01-01..

version w
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-02-01
  members + [ana] lives 2026-02-01..

ask q: count(k in volunteers on 2026-06-01), count(k in members on 2026-06-01)
=== expect
q: (1, 1)
  cut 2026-10-18
